\section*{Cross-Reference to Related Applications}
This application relates to high-throughput telemetry ingestion systems,
including AXI4-Stream fabrics, SPI sensor capture subsystems, and unified
scientific simulation engines.

\section*{Field of the Invention}
The invention pertains to hardware telemetry ingestion systems, specifically
AXI4-Stream data pipelines and SPI sensor capture architectures used in
scientific, cosmological, and unified-field simulation environments.

\section*{Background of the Invention}
Existing scientific hardware platforms rely on fragmented ingestion pipelines
with limited throughput, high latency, and insufficient synchronization across
heterogeneous sensors. Conventional SPI capture systems lack deterministic
framing, metadata tagging, and high-speed bridging into AXI4-Stream fabrics.
No prior art discloses a unified ingestion architecture combining:
\begin{itemize}
    \item multi-channel SPI capture,
    \item AXI4-Stream packetization,
    \item deterministic metadata tagging,
    \item CRC-based integrity verification,
    \item low-jitter clock synchronization,
    \item high-throughput DMA buffering.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Summary of the Invention}
The invention provides a unified hardware architecture comprising:
\begin{itemize}
    \item a multi-channel SPI sensor capture subsystem,
    \item a packet formatter generating AXI4-Stream frames,
    \item a metadata injection engine,
    \item CRC integrity verification,
    \item an AXI4-Stream switch fabric,
    \item a DMA engine for DDR buffering,
    \item deterministic timing and low-jitter clock domains.
\end{itemize}

