\section*{Detailed Description of the Invention}

\subsection*{SPI Sensor Capture Subsystem}
The SPI subsystem supports:
\begin{itemize}
    \item SPI Modes 0--3,
    \item clock rates up to 50\,MHz,
    \item 8-, 16-, and 32-bit word widths,
    \item up to 8 independent sensor channels.
\end{itemize}

SPI frames are assembled with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item start-of-frame (SOF),
    \item end-of-frame (EOF),
    \item CRC-16/CRC-32,
    \item timestamp metadata,
    \item sensor ID tagging.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{AXI4-Stream Packet Formatter}
SPI frames are converted into AXI4-Stream packets using:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{TDATA} for payload,
    \item \texttt{TUSER} for metadata,
    \item \texttt{TLAST} for frame boundaries,
    \item \texttt{TKEEP} for byte masking.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{AXI4-Stream Fabric}
The AXI fabric includes:
\begin{itemize}
    \item AXI stream switch,
    \item AXI DMA engine,
    \item DDR4/DDR5 memory controller,
    \item deterministic latency constraints.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Clocking and Timing}
Clock domains include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 100\,MHz reference oscillator ($<0.5$\,ps jitter),
    \item 250\,MHz AXI fabric clock,
    \item 50\,MHz SPI clock,
    \item CDC FIFOs for domain crossing.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Integrity Verification}
CRC engines validate all SPI frames before AXI packetization. Metadata includes:
\begin{itemize}
    \item sensor ID,
    \item timestamp,
    \item CRC status,
    \item channel index.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Claims}

\begin{enumerate}

\item A telemetry ingestion system comprising:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item a multi-channel SPI sensor capture subsystem configured to receive
        sensor data at up to 50\,MHz;
        \item a packet formatter configured to assemble SPI frames into AXI4-Stream
        packets with SOF, EOF, CRC, and metadata;
        \item an AXI4-Stream fabric configured to transport said packets using
        \texttt{TVALID}, \texttt{TREADY}, \texttt{TDATA}, \texttt{TUSER}, and
        \texttt{TLAST};
        \item a DMA engine configured to buffer AXI packets into DDR memory;
        \item a clock distribution network providing low-jitter timing domains.
    \end{enumerate}

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein the SPI subsystem supports 8 independent
channels.

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein the packet formatter injects metadata
including sensor ID, timestamp, CRC status, and channel index.

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein CRC-16 or CRC-32 is applied to each SPI frame.

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein AXI packetization uses 128- or 256-bit
\texttt{TDATA} widths.

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein end-to-end latency from SPI capture to AXI
ingress is less than $5\,\mu\text{s}$.

\item The system of Claim~1 wherein jitter on the AXI fabric clock is less than
$5$\,ps.

\item A method for telemetry ingestion comprising:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item capturing SPI sensor frames,
        \item assembling said frames with SOF, EOF, and CRC,
        \item converting said frames into AXI4-Stream packets,
        \item injecting metadata into \texttt{TUSER},
        \item transmitting packets through an AXI fabric,
        \item buffering packets via DMA into DDR memory.
    \end{enumerate}

\item A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that cause
a processor to perform the method of Claim~8.

\item A unified telemetry architecture comprising any combination of the
elements described in Claims~1--9.

\end{enumerate}

\section*{Abstract}
A hardware telemetry ingestion system comprising a multi-channel SPI sensor
capture subsystem, an AXI4-Stream packet formatter, a metadata injection engine,
a CRC integrity module, an AXI4-Stream fabric, and a DMA buffering subsystem.
The invention provides deterministic, high-throughput, low-latency ingestion
suitable for scientific and cosmological simulation engines.

